    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d190">

                <pb facs="0275" n="261" sameAs="frus:frus1948v06/pg261"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BC
                    Indonesia/6–2348: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Batavia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Livengood</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Batavia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-06-23">June 23, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>555. Gocus 321. GOC has telegraphed report to SC<anchor n="1" xml:id="d190-f1"/> giving factual background
                    suspension negotiations and ending with statement from <pb facs="0276" n="262"
                        xml:id="pg262"/>
                    NethDel letter June 22 stating NethDel authorized proceed with discussions
                    with RepubDel.</p>
                <p>Addendum to report to be telegraphed today stating RepubDel placed US-Australian working paper on agenda today’s
                    steering committee, NethDel rejected it, and
                        GOC, which called upon render decision in
                    matter, unable reach decision (US and Australian voting for retention Belgium
                    against) and appealed parties consult together in effort agree upon formula
                    permitting consideration paper as basis for discussions. Signed Dubois.</p>
                <p>Department pass Hague.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d190-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Livengood</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d190-f1" n="1" xml:id="d190-f1-content">
                <p>For texts of two telegrams to the Security Council, June 22, see SC, <hi rendition="#italic">3rd yr., Suppl.</hi>
                    (June), pp. 147, 150 (documents S/850 and S/850/Add.1).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d190-f2" n="2" xml:id="d190-f2-content">
                <p>This was done the same day.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
